---
description: Keep docs/*.md current when adding or changing game systems
alwaysApply: true
---

Before changing a system, read `docs/README.md` and the matching topic MD.
Those files say where the code lives and which invariants apply.

When you add or change a function, also update the docs in the same change:

- Existing system → edit its topic MD (files, entry points, invariants, tests).
- New system → extend a topic MD or add `docs/<topic>.md` and register it in
  `docs/README.md` and the table in root `AGENTS.md`.
- New `GameCommand` or `GameSnapshot` field → `docs/multiplayer.md` and
  `docs/saves.md`.
- New balancing key → mention it in the topic MD; keep values in
  `src/game/simulationConfig.ts`.
- Player-visible behaviour or controls → root `README.md`.

A feature is not finished if new modules, kinds or commands are missing from
the documentation map.
